{"status":"success","data":[{"site":{"siteid":30965,"sitename":"Palomaa","sitedescription":"Small mire located close to the northern limit of pine forest in eastern Finnish Lapland. To the south, forest areas are dominated almost exclusively by Scots Pine (Pinus sylvestris) while, to the north, the regional vegetation type is mountain birch woodland (Betula pubescens ssp. czerepanovii).","sitenotes":"String fen in which the strings are not well developed but rather occur as Sphagnum fuscum hummocks with Betula nana, Empetrum nigrum, Vaccinium uliginosum, V. oxycoccus, Ledum palustre, Andromeda polifolia and Rubus chamaemorus, separated by flark areas dominated by Eriophorum vaginatum, Trichophorum caespitosum and Carex spp. There is one extensive pool, some smaller areas of standing water and a stream that drains the mire towards the east.","geography":"{\"type\":\"Point\",\"crs\":{\"type\":\"name\",\"properties\":{\"name\":\"EPSG:4326\"}},\"coordinates\":[27.19048,69.2778]}","altitude":200,"collectionunitid":42184,"collectionunit":"Palomaa core","handle":"PALOMAA","unittype":"Core","datasets":[{"doi":[],"agerange":[],"database":"European Pollen Database","datasetid":58529,"datasetpi":[{"initials":"T.","contactid":9628,"firstname":"Tomasz","familyname":"Goslar","contactname":"Goslar, Tomasz"}],"datasettype":"geochronologic","datasetnotes":null,"recdatecreated":"2024-04-11T13:38:58"},{"doi":["10.21233/d49m-jd45","10.21233/MKRP-9818"],"agerange":[{"units":"Calendar years BP","ageold":878.26,"ageyoung":-54.58}],"database":"European Pollen Database","datasetid":58530,"datasetpi":[{"initials":"A.","contactid":18392,"firstname":"Andreas","familyname":"Lücke","contactname":"Lücke, Andreas"},{"initials":"F.","contactid":4065,"firstname":"Friederike","familyname":"Wagner-Cremer","contactname":"Wagner-Cremer, Friederike"},{"initials":"H.","contactid":17070,"firstname":"Heidi","familyname":"Hyyppä","contactname":"Hyyppä, Heidi"},{"initials":"K.","contactid":19530,"firstname":"